# What must never enter an image layer.
#
# This file is a security control, not a build optimisation. `COPY . .` in the
# runtime stage would otherwise bake in whatever happens to be in the working
# tree — and .env is gitignored, so it is exactly the file a developer has
# locally and never thinks about. Two things go wrong at once:
#
#   * the SECRET_KEY, database password and any object-storage credentials in it
#     ship inside the image, readable by anyone who can pull it;
#   * django-environ reads it at boot IN PREFERENCE to the real environment, so
#     the container silently runs on a developer's machine-specific settings.
#     That is how this was found: the image inherited a macOS Homebrew
#     GDAL_LIBRARY_PATH and died on `collectstatic` with a dylib it could never
#     have had.
#
# private-media/ is on the list for the obvious reason: it holds verification
# evidence in development.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

.git/
.github/
.gitignore

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

node_modules/
# Rebuilt inside the image by the asset stage — a host copy would shadow it.
build/
static/css/
staticfiles/

media/
private-media/
.pytest-private-media/

.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
docs/
